<title>USA: Greenspan reiterates he opposes capital gains tax.</title>
<headline>Greenspan reiterates he opposes capital gains tax.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan on Tuesday reiterated his opposition to the tax on capital gains, saying that it limits economic growth.</p>
<p>&quot;I've always advocated a tax structure which would maximize economic growth,&quot; Greenspan told a House subcommittee during his Humphrey-Hawkins testimony. He said reductions in capital gains taxes and marginal tax rates were elements in such a structure.</p>
</text>
